---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="How the Pathfinder pilot handles your data: no accounts, no tracking, and preferences stored only in your browser.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy" lede="The pilot collects as little as possible. Here is exactly what happens to your data." />
  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>What the pilot stores</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>No accounts, and no analytics or advertising trackers.</li>
        <li>The eligibility check and cost planner work inside your browser. The marks and amounts you type aren’t sent anywhere.</li>
        <li>Your theme choice and daily question count are stored only in your own browser and never sent to us.</li>
        <li>Questions you ask are answered inside your browser from our published fact store. They are not sent to a server.</li>
        <li>The comparison and cost tools fetch public exchange rates from the European Central Bank feed (via Frankfurter), with no personal data attached.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="signups">If you join the waitlist or ask for change alerts</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>We collect only what you give us: whether you’re a student or a parent, an email or WhatsApp number, the countries you’re interested in and, for the waitlist, the level and start date you choose. We also note which page you signed up on.</li>
        <li>Your sign-up only counts after you confirm it from the link we send to that email or WhatsApp number, so nobody can sign you up without you.</li>
        <li>We use it only to tell you about what you signed up for: Premium opening for your countries, or a change to a rule or figure for a country you follow.</li>
        <li>We record that you agreed, when you confirmed, and which version of the wording you agreed to.</li>
        <li>We don’t knowingly collect details from anyone under 18; a parent or guardian can sign up instead. If we learn a sign-up came from someone under 18, we delete it.</li>
        <li>Every message includes a link that deletes your sign-up straight away. Sign-ups are deleted automatically after a year. You can also ask for a copy of your details; the contact for that will be published here before sign-ups are switched on.</li>
        <li>The sign-up service doesn’t keep logs of who signed up beyond the record itself.</li>
        <li>We never sell or share your details, and never pass them to universities, agents or lenders.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>When accounts launch</h2>
      <p>
        Accounts will come with consent capture, data export and deletion you can do yourself, and verifiable parental consent for
        users under 18. We are designing them to India’s Digital Personal Data Protection Act and Rules, GDPR and UK GDPR, and
        Singapore’s PDPA, among others. This page will be updated before any personal data is collected.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
